WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:03.439
Some characters are destined to steal the
show.

00:00:03.439 --> 00:00:08.380
But when it comes time to cast roles, crazy
things can happen, and it's impossible to

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:12.020
predict who will end up in front of the cameras
when they start rolling.

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:17.760
It may be hard to imagine, but some of your
favorite movies and TV shows almost featured

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:20.600
someone else entirely in the leading role.

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:24.420
Here's a list of roles everyone in Hollywood
wanted to play.

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:26.160
Young Han Solo

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:31.900
Casting the original Han Solo was nearly as
tough as making the kessel run in under 12

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:32.400
parsecs.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:37.420
So when Lucasfilm and Disney announced they'd
be expanding the Star Wars universe with a

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:43.219
full slate of standalone films — including
a "young Han Solo" prequel directed by Phil

00:00:43.219 --> 00:00:49.680
Lord and Christopher Miller — every twentysomething
male actor in the galaxy lined up to audition.

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:55.589
Among the big names: Whiplash's Miles Teller,
Ansel Elgort from The Fault in Our Stars,

00:00:55.589 --> 00:00:59.280
Neighbors star Zac Efron, and Brooklyn's Emory
Cohen.

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:05.580
Sources claim over 2,500 actors either met
with casting or submitted tapes before Hail,

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:11.590
Caesar! breakout actor Alden Ehrenreich was
ultimately cast in the hotly anticipated film,

00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:13.760
which will fly into theaters in 2018.

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:15.920
Just don't get cocky, kid.

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:19.960
Of course, that wasn't the only Star Wars
role to be hotly contested...

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:21.020
Rey

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:28.000
A long time ago in a galaxy far, far away,
Lucasfilm decided to make a third Star Wars

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:31.640
trilogy and needed a brand new hero to anchor
it.

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:35.490
Director J.J. Abrams and the casting team
launched an extensive search for the right

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:39.540
person to play Rey, the mysterious orphan
at the heart of The Force Awakens.

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:46.080
Oscar nominee Saoirse Ronan auditioned, apparently
having a blast "pretending to take out a lightsaber."

00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:51.290
Elizabeth Olsen and Shailene Woodley were
rumored to have auditioned for the part as

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:55.650
well, but Abrams was dead set on casting a
fresh face.

00:01:55.650 --> 00:02:01.270
Newcomer Daisy Ridley nabbed the role after
five auditions, including one tearful screen

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:03.660
test that blew Abrams away.

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:06.220
The Force is strong with that one.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:07.880
Wonder Woman

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:14.240
Hollywood has tried and failed for decades
to bring Wonder Woman to the big screen.

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:19.440
Along the way, quite a few of the film industry's
biggest stars have expressed interest in putting

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:25.090
on her iconic bracelets, including Sandra
Bullock, Mad Men's Christina Hendricks, former

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:32.170
Bond Girl Olga Kurylenko, and even Katie Holmes
— who's no stranger to the DC Comics universe.

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:37.900
When Warner Bros. finally decided to cast
Wonder Woman for 2016's Batman v Superman,

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:39.900
the casting description read:

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:43.380
"Tall, brunette, athletic and exotic."

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:50.060
Israeli actress Gal Gadot won the role — and
a shot at solo cinematic stardom with Wonder

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:50.560
Woman,

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:52.980
James Bond

00:02:54.300 --> 00:03:00.040
Betting on who will become the next 007 has
become a national pastime for bookies in the

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:04.630
U.K. Six actors have portrayed the world's
most famous spy on the big screen, but every

00:03:04.630 --> 00:03:10.180
time the role is vacated, a new crop of hot
British actors hope to fill Bond's perfectly-tailored

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:10.860
suits.

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:15.760
Among those over the years who've wanted their
martinis shaken and not stirred:

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:20.670
Michael Caine, Liam Neeson, Ralph Fiennes,
Colin Firth, and Clive Owen.

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:26.380
Current Bond Daniel Craig has been hesitant
to confirm his participation in another film

00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:30.410
after the success — and stress — of four
films in the role.

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:35.110
Until he does, a few favorite candidates have
emerged as his possible successor: Luther's

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:41.060
Idris Elba, Thor baddie Tom Hiddleston, Tom
Hardy, and Homeland's Damien Lewis.

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:45.630
Even X-Files star Gillian Anderson wants to
put her spin on the role.

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:48.980
Who will be the next secret agent to carry
a license to kill?

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:50.920
Only time will tell.

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:53.900
Christian Grey and Anastasia Steele

00:03:54.300 --> 00:04:00.180
When it came time to cast the big-screen adaptation
of erotic bestseller Fifty Shades of Grey,

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:02.310
fans of the series, as well as author E.L.

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:07.180
James, had plenty of opinions regarding who
should play the lead roles.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:12.640
Fans campaigned especially hard for Matt Bomer,
Alexis Bledel, and Ian Somerhalder, among

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:13.140
others.

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:18.840
James was partial to Shailene Woodley, who
passed because of her commitment to the Divergent

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:19.340
franchise.

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:25.639
Other names entered seriously into the mix:
Oscar winner Alicia Vikander, True Blood's

00:04:25.639 --> 00:04:30.789
Alexander Skarsgard, Cara Delevingne, and
Oscar nominee Felicity Jones.

00:04:30.789 --> 00:04:35.529
Sons of Anarchy's Charlie Hunnam was originally
cast as Grey opposite Dakota Johnson before

00:04:35.529 --> 00:04:39.879
dropping out and being replaced by Irish actor
Jamie Dornan.

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:42.000
Guess Hunnam got too tied up.

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:43.460
Harry Potter

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:48.770
To cast the Boy Who Lived, Warner Bros. put
out an open call on the internet for Harry

00:04:48.770 --> 00:04:55.240
Potter lookalikes, and over 40,000 kids sent
in audition materials in hopes of being chosen.

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:56.520
Author J.K.

00:04:56.520 --> 00:05:01.800
Rowling's one stipulation was the cast be
British, eliminating Sorcerer's Stone director

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:05.560
Chris Columbus' initial first choice: Stepmom's
Liam Aiken.

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:10.980
But plenty of other young American actors
expressed interest, including the Sixth Sense's

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:16.199
Haley Joel Osment and Jonathan Lipnicki of
Jerry Maguire fame.

00:05:16.199 --> 00:05:20.460
Though he wound up playing Draco, even Tom
Felton initially auditioned for the parts

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:22.100
of both Harry and Ron.

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:26.820
Of course, now it's impossible to imagine
anyone but Daniel Radcliffe as the boy wizard.

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:28.300
Clarice Starling

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:33.780
Hannibal Lecter actually never said "Hello
Clarice" in the movie Silence of the Lambs

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:34.780
- really!

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:41.279
And Clarice almost wasn't the Clarice we remember
so well had late director Jonathan Demme had

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:41.780
his way.

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:47.000
Though Jodie Foster campaigned heavily to
get the role, she wasn't anywhere in Demme's

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:47.500
shortlist.

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:52.420
Michelle Pfeiffer was the first choice, having
just worked with Demme on Married to the Mob,

00:05:52.439 --> 00:05:57.210
but she was uncomfortable with the movie's
subject matter and ultimately passed.

00:05:57.210 --> 00:06:01.461
Meg Ryan was also considered thanks to her
popularity coming off a string of hits, but

00:06:01.461 --> 00:06:07.400
she too passed, apparently "offended" Demme
even thought of her for such a gruesome project.

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:13.339
Laura Dern gave such an impressive audition,
Demme said she was "it," but studios weren't

00:06:13.339 --> 00:06:18.099
comfortable with the still relatively unknown
actress carrying such a big project.

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:21.240
So he gave the role to Foster — who went
on to win an Oscar.

00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:23.440
Katniss Everdeen

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:29.800
After the massive success of the Hunger Games
book trilogy, there was no shortage of actresses

00:06:29.800 --> 00:06:33.729
looking to score the highly coveted lead role
of Katniss Everdeen.

00:06:33.729 --> 00:06:38.270
Emily Browning, best known for her role in
Sucker Punch and The Uninvited, was a top

00:06:38.270 --> 00:06:40.060
contender for the part.

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:45.159
Saoirse Ronan, who starred in Hanna with Cate
Blanchett, was also a strong choice with her

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:49.160
background in hand-to-hand combat and penchant
for athletic roles.

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:54.720
Also on the list were Abigail Breslin from
Little Miss Sunshine and Hailee Steinfeld

00:06:54.729 --> 00:06:55.729
of True Grit.

00:06:55.729 --> 00:07:00.500
Of course, Katniss went to Jennifer Lawrence,
and the rest was movie history.

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:02.080
Amy Dunne

00:07:02.660 --> 00:07:09.580
Anyone who read Gone Girl knows the casting
for the character of Amy Dunne had to be perfect.

00:07:09.580 --> 00:07:14.529
This highly sought after part was actively
pursued by Natalie Portman, Charlize Theron,

00:07:14.529 --> 00:07:15.770
and Olivia Wilde.

00:07:15.770 --> 00:07:20.539
Portman, the Oscar-winning actress best known
for her turn in Black Swan, would have brought

00:07:20.539 --> 00:07:25.969
a multi-layered performance, while Charlize
Theron's stunningly disturbed turn as Mary

00:07:25.969 --> 00:07:31.599
Ann Lomax in The Devil's Advocate with Keanu
Reeves proved she could have nailed this role

00:07:31.599 --> 00:07:33.309
alongside Ben Affleck.

00:07:33.309 --> 00:07:39.050
Finally, Olivia Wilde, no stranger to carrying
a film as the deranged Zoe in The Lazarus

00:07:39.050 --> 00:07:42.460
Effect, had the looks and the chops for the
role of Amy.

00:07:42.780 --> 00:07:47.400
It ultimately went to Rosamund Pike, who turned
out to be the perfect choice.

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:48.740
Vivian Ward

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:53.740
For awhile, it seemed like every actress in
Hollywood was clamoring to play the hooker

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:57.740
with a heart of gold in what many consider
to be Gary Marshall's masterpiece.

00:07:58.280 --> 00:08:03.200
Meg Ryan was initially offered the part opposite
Richard Gere, but had to decline the offer

00:08:03.320 --> 00:08:04.990
as she had scheduling conflicts.

00:08:04.990 --> 00:08:10.900
A string of other actresses nearly took the
opportunity to play Vivian but had concerns

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:15.210
with the subject matter, including Michelle
Pfeiffer and Daryl Hannah.

00:08:15.210 --> 00:08:18.940
Julia Roberts ultimately landed the career-making
part.

00:08:19.780 --> 00:08:21.020
Michael Corleone

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:25.659
Believe it or not, Paramount Pictures' first
choice for the compelling Godfather franchise

00:08:25.659 --> 00:08:27.289
was not Al Pacino.

00:08:27.289 --> 00:08:31.740
It's hard not to picture him in the leading
role, but at one point Jack Nicholson was

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:34.240
wanted to play Michael Corleone.

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:38.780
Warren Beatty and Dustin Hoffman also expressed
interest in playing the role and made it far

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:40.839
along in the casting process.

00:08:40.839 --> 00:08:46.180
Meanwhile, director Francis Ford Coppola nearly
pulled out of the project as he fought Paramount

00:08:46.180 --> 00:08:50.420
executives over casting Marlon Brando as Don
Vito Corleone.

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:51.420
Batman

00:08:52.060 --> 00:08:56.740
As far as Batman movies go, Tim Burton's first
Batman flick is legendary.

00:08:57.180 --> 00:09:02.320
In the 1980s, every leading man in Hollywood
actively sought an audition to be a part of

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:07.000
what was undoubtedly going to be a hit franchise
with a stellar paycheck.

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:09.920
Can you imagine your favorite Ghostbuster
as Batman?

00:09:10.220 --> 00:09:14.620
That's right: Bill Murray was reportedly considered
for the batsuit.

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:19.220
Mel Gibson was rumored too, as were Charlie
Sheen and Alec Baldwin.

00:09:19.220 --> 00:09:24.260
After all that, Michael Keaton was the lucky
guy who eventually donned the cape and cowl.

00:09:24.700 --> 00:09:25.420
Ferris Bueller

00:09:26.060 --> 00:09:31.060
John Hughes reportedly wrote Ferris Bueller's
Day Off with Matthew Broderick in mind, but

00:09:31.060 --> 00:09:33.060
other actors had to be considered.

00:09:33.060 --> 00:09:36.399
Johnny Depp was initially offered the role
but ultimately turned it down.

00:09:36.399 --> 00:09:41.740
Jim Carrey was also rumored to be in the mix,
but after conducting his studio-mandated search,

00:09:41.740 --> 00:09:46.959
Hughes returned to Broderick, the guy he'd
wanted for the part all along — and in hindsight,

00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:49.220
it's pretty obvious he had the right idea.

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:50.920
Dr. Evil

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:56.400
Who doesn't get a kick out of this super '60s-themed
spy comedy?

00:09:56.780 --> 00:10:01.760
Up until a scheduling conflict arose with
the production of Liar, Liar, comedy superstar

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:07.500
Jim Carrey was set to play Dr. Evil in Austin
Powers: International Man of Mystery.

00:10:08.020 --> 00:10:12.760
Stuck for an actor to fill the crucial role,
star and creator Mike Myers decided to don

00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:16.500
the bald cap and play Austin Powers' nemesis
himself.

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:17.880
Rachel Green

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:23.440
Easily one of the most popular sitcoms of
all time, Friends catapulted every actor involved

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:27.580
to fame, most notably Jennifer Aniston, who
played Rachel Green.

00:10:27.780 --> 00:10:32.139
Many young hopefuls auditioned for the role
that would eventually inspire one of the most

00:10:32.139 --> 00:10:34.430
imitated hairstyles of all time.

00:10:34.430 --> 00:10:39.350
At first, the producers expressed strong interest
in actress Tea Leoni.

00:10:39.350 --> 00:10:44.399
But as when Aniston passed on an opportunity
at Saturday Night Live to sign on for the

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:47.960
sitcom, the rest became Must-See TV history.

00:10:48.700 --> 00:10:49.780
Scarlett O'Hara

00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:54.360
It may very well be the most famous casting
search of all time.

00:10:54.370 --> 00:11:00.139
In an effort to build anticipation for the
1939 big screen adaptation of Margaret Mitchell's

00:11:00.139 --> 00:11:06.240
epic novel Gone with the Wind, producer David
O. Selznick decided to make his hunt for spunky

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:09.580
heroine Scarlett O'Hara a national obsession.

00:11:09.950 --> 00:11:14.600
According to an Entertainment Weekly article,
he had fans writing impassioned letters on

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:21.129
behalf of their favorite actresses and a whistle-stop
tour of the South looking for unknown talent.

00:11:21.129 --> 00:11:27.930
TCM.com says that MGM spent two years trying
to cast the role, seeing 1,400 actresses and

00:11:27.930 --> 00:11:33.730
testing the likes of Katharine Hepburn, Tallulah
Bankhead, Bette Davis, Paulette Goddard, and

00:11:33.730 --> 00:11:34.260
Joan Crawford.

00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:39.440
Filming had already begun on the burning of
Atlanta scene when relatively unknown British

00:11:39.440 --> 00:11:44.720
actress Vivien Leigh was cast just days before
principal photography was set to begin, ending

00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:49.400
a search nearly as melodramatic as Scarlett
herself.

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:50.400
Thanks for watching!

00:11:50.720 --> 00:11:53.459
Click The Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:11:53.459 --> 00:11:55.449
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

